/* <version> — C++ [version.syn].
 *
 * The feature-test macros, and nothing else. It exists so a program can
 * ask what this library has WITHOUT including the header that might not
 * be there: `#include <version>` then `#if __cpp_lib_ranges` is the
 * only portable way to test, because including `<ranges>` to find out
 * whether `<ranges>` exists does not work.
 *
 * Every macro below is defined because the feature is implemented here,
 * and one that is absent is absent because the feature is. The value is
 * the date the paper was adopted, which is how a program distinguishes
 * an early implementation from a complete one. Where this library is
 * narrower than the paper, the macro is left out rather than claimed --
 * a false __cpp_lib_ macro is worse than a missing one, because it
 * turns a compile error into a silent wrong answer in the branch it
 * selects.
 */
